<%- include('partials/header', { title: 'Backups' }) %>

<h1>Data Backup</h1>

<div class="card">
  <h2>Download a Full Backup</h2>
  <p class="muted">
    This downloads a single .zip file containing every return, its full status history,
    staff accounts (without passwords), and every uploaded photo/video - a complete,
    independent snapshot you can keep somewhere safe (e.g. a shared company drive).
  </p>
  <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/backup/download">Download Backup (.zip)</a>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>Automatic Daily Backup</h2>
  <p class="muted">
    On top of downloading one manually above, the exact same backup can be emailed out
    automatically once a day - no need to remember to do it yourself. Turn it on for whichever
    staff should receive it from the <strong>Email Notifications</strong> area on the
    <a href="/users">Staff Accounts</a> page (look for the "Daily Backup" column). It only sends
    while at least one person is opted in - nobody is opted in by default.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>Good habits</h2>
  <p class="muted">A few sensible ways to use this:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Download one now, and make it a habit every week or month.</li>
    <li>Keep at least one copy somewhere other than this computer (e.g. shared drive, email to yourself).</li>
    <li>Grab one before any big change - a Render plan change, a big app update, etc.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="muted">
    This is a safety net on top of your hosting, not a replacement for it. If the app is still
    on Render's free plan, its data can be wiped by every restart regardless of how often you
    back up - ask about switching to a paid plan with a permanent disk if that hasn't been done yet.
  </p>
</div>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
